{{!
Copy of the swagger-codegen-generators JavaSpring (handlebars) model template with the
JsonNullable / NotUndefined helper imports dropped. Both validationMode values (strict and
loose) pull them in, but this module has no required+nullable fields, so they were only
forcing a jackson-databind-nullable dependency and io.swagger.configuration support classes
into a published library. See pojo.mustache, which drops the matching @NotUndefined marker.

Branches that the generator options in build.gradle can never reach are stripped, so this
template only renders what it actually emits. It assumes jakarta=true, useBeanValidation=true
and validationMode=strict (the codegen defaults), and that serializableModel and withXml stay
unset. That drops the javax.* validation imports, java.io.Serializable and the Jackson/JAXB
XML imports. Changing any of those options means restoring the matching branch from upstream.
Original template is here:
https://github.com/swagger-api/swagger-codegen-generators/blob/master/src/main/resources/handlebars/JavaSpring/model.mustache
}}
